<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2c-xichang ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2C / unknown payload (Xichang LC-3) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Event times: CALT TYPICAL LM-2C sequence via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征二号丙: S1 cutoff 146.5 s, sep 148.0 s, fairing 161.3 s, S2 main cutoff 338.1 s, vernier cutoff 542.7 s (payload sep 545.7 s).
Azimuth 136.38 deg: great-circle bearing from pad to NOTAM ZJSA A5624/26 danger-area centroid 18.379N 111.575E (1466 km) (https://www.space-notices.com/); implies i~52.6 deg.
Payload and orbit unpublished (LL2): final altitude 500 km circular ASSUMED.
T0: LL2 NET 2026-11-05T16:00:00Z (window 15:52-16:16Z = Thu 5 Nov 8:00 am PST).
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times, final = assumed orbit): 0:0, 146.5:71.5, 148:73.6, 161.3:92.8, 338.1:361.6, 542.7:500
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.330 km/s (circular v at 500 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+542.7 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 28.247059N 102.029008E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=136.38 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-05T16:00:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
